  "summary": "The x86-64 kernel without the i386 ABI, built with IA32=0 or booted with ia32_emulation=0, refuses an i386 program's exec with ENOEXEC and int $0x80 with SIGSEGV, as Linux does, still runs 32-bit code in a 64-bit process, and names a resumed sleep's wait do_syscall_64; the program is tests/pure64probe.c",
